{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":20209,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,4]],"date-time":"2022-04-04T01:01:17Z","timestamp":1649034077665},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2020,3,23]]},"group-title":"pico","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>\n        &amp;lt;p&amp;gt;We investigated the processes beneath the Avacha volcano using mantle peridotite xenoliths&amp;amp;#160; the with the EPMA, electronic microscope and ICP methods and&amp;amp;#160; numeric modeling of the mass transfer accounting the melt fluid reactions with peridotites&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;The decompression melting processes&amp;amp;#160; in peridotites beneath Avachinsky volcano (Kamchatka) are associated with seismic events. After the reactions with the Si, Ca, Na, K&amp;amp;#160; from partial&amp;amp;#160; melts associated&amp;amp;#160; with&amp;amp;#160; the&amp;amp;#160; subduction related fluids the spinel and orthopyroxene were melted and essentially clinopyroxene veins were formed. Secondary crystals growth in the mantle xenoliths (with melt and fluid inclusions) are associated possibly with&amp;amp;#160; the fluids appeared&amp;amp;#160; due to retrograde boiling of the magma chamber beneath the volcano.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;The processes of sublimation and recrystallization of&amp;amp;#160; Avacha harzburgites was investigated at the facility in the Institute of&amp;amp;#160; Nuclear Physics (Novosibirsk, Russia), which generates high-density electron beams and makes it possible to obtain boiling ultrabasic and basic liquids and condensates of magmatic gas on the surface of&amp;amp;#160; harzburgite.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Results of&amp;amp;#160; experiments provides a satisfactory explanation for the observed local heterophase alterations within ultramafic rocks that have experienced multistage deformation beneath volcanoes of the Kamchatka volcanic front.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Mathematical model of convective heating and metasomatic reactions in harzburgites were modeled using the&amp;amp;#160; Selector PC thermodynamic software. The obtained virtual dynamic patterns of metasomatic zoning across the mantle wedge show&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; how&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; composition&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; variations&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; of&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; fluids&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; and&amp;amp;#160; PT&amp;amp;#160; conditions&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; at&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; their&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; sources&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; influence&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; the&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; facies&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; of&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; metasomatized&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; mantle&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; wedge harzburgite.&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; Such processes are apparently common to seismically&amp;amp;#160; deformed&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; permeable&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; lithosphere&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; above&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; magma&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160; reservoirs.&amp;amp;#160;&amp;amp;#160;&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;There are two regions fluid filtration conditions under the Avachinsky volcano which are regulated by the tectonic conditions. The lower field where compression conditions prevail. And the upper field, where the prevailing tensile conditions and intense seismic destruction of the rocks of the crust and upper mantle. The heat flux distribution shows the manifestation of the convective heating mechanism in the earth's crust over the most permeable fault zones.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;The study of the composition of the gas phases and melt inclusions suggests that the partial melting of metasomatized ultrabasites occurs in the range of 1150 &amp;amp;#176; C &amp;lt;T &amp;lt;1200 &amp;amp;#176; C.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;In accord with the composition of the glassy phase in the melt inclusions of spinel crystals, the harzburgite metasomatism in the local melting sites is associated with brine melts that bringing Ca, K, Na, Si. C. The work was &amp;amp;#239;&amp;amp;#172;&amp;amp;#129;nancially supported by the Russian Foundation for Basic Research, Grants No. 16-29-15131, 16-01-00729.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;References&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Arai S., Ishimaru S. Insights into Petrologycal Characteristics of the Lithosphere Mantle Wedge beneath Arcs through Peridotite Xenoliths: a Review.\/\/ J. Petrol., 2008. V.49(4), 359-395.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Tomilenko A.A., Kovyazin S.V., Sharapov V.N., Timina T.Yu., Kuzmin D.V. Metasomatic recrystallization and melting of ultrabasic rocks of mantle wedge beneath Avacha Volcano, Kamchatka \/\/ ACROFI III and TBG XIV Abstracts Volume \/ SB RAS IGM, Novosibirsk: Publishing House of SB RAS, 2010, p. 248-249.&amp;lt;\/p&amp;gt;\n        <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.5194\/egusphere-egu2020-362","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,3,9]],"date-time":"2020-03-09T12:31:46Z","timestamp":1583757106000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Features of heat and mass transfer processes under the Avachinsky volcano (Kamchatka)"],"prefix":"10.5194","author":[{"given":"Grigory","family":"Kuznetsov","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Victor","family":"Sharapov","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"3145","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2020,3,23]],"date-time":"2020-03-23T16:21:23Z","timestamp":1584980483000},"score":28.053959,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/meetingorganizer.copernicus.org\/EGU2020\/EGU2020-362.html"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2020,3,23]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5194\/egusphere-egu2020-362","published":{"date-parts":[[2020,3,23]]},"subtype":"other"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,1]],"date-time":"2026-04-01T23:45:20Z","timestamp":1775087120975,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":15,"publisher":"Geophysical Survey of the Russian Academy of Sciences - GS RAS","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["RJS"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,21]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>The gravitational interaction between the Earth, the Moon and the Sun is of a periodic nature, acting on a global scale and causing terrestrial and sea tides. The study of seismicity variations associated with lunisolar tides is a traditional task of seismology. The purpose of the presented study is to study the relationship between the number of volcanic earthquakes and the level of tidal loads using the example of Avachinsky volcano, located in the southeast of Kamchatka. The effect of an increase in the intensity of the flow of volcanic earthquakes with an increase in the level of the sea tide and ebb has been established. Recordings of the vertical component of the mass displacement channel of the CMG-3TB seismometer were used in the work.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.35540\/2686-7907.2023.1.06","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,28]],"date-time":"2023-03-28T11:31:33Z","timestamp":1680003093000},"page":"89-95","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Tidal effects in the seismicity of Avachinsky volcano"],"prefix":"10.35540","volume":"5","author":[{"given":"Yu.V.","family":"Shevchenko","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"KB GS RAS"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"V.V.","family":"Yakovenko","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"KB GS RAS"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"19389","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,21]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref0","unstructured":"Arachnoid.com. (2022). Tides Home Page. Retrieved from https:\/\/arachnoid.com\/tides"},{"key":"ref1","unstructured":"Balesta, S.E., Gontovaia, L.I., Kargapol\u2019tsev, A.A., Pushkarev, V.G., & Seniukov, S.L. (1988). [Seismic model of Avachinsky volcano (according to KMPVGSZ data)]. Vulkanologiia i seismologiia [Volcanology and Seismology], 2, 43-55. (In Russ.)."},{"key":"ref2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","unstructured":"Chebrov, V.N., Droznin, D.V., Kugaenko, Yu.A., Levina, V.I., Seniukov, S.L., Sergeev, V.A., Shevchenko, Yu.V., & Iashchuk, V.V. (2013). The system of detailed seismological observations in Kamchatka in 2011. Journal of Volcanology and Seismology, 7(1), 16-36. DOI: 10.1134\/ S0742046313010028","DOI":"10.1134\/s0742046313010028"},{"key":"ref3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","unstructured":"Chebrova, A.Iu., Chemarev, E.A., Matveenko, E.A., & Chebrov, D.V. (2020). [Unified information system of seismological data in the Kamchatka Branch of the GS RAS: principles of organization, main elements, key functions]. Geofizicheskie issledovaniia [Geophysical Research], 21(3), 66-91. (In Russ.). DOI: 10.21455\/ gr2020.3-5. EDN: QQHRZU","DOI":"10.21455\/gr2020.3-5"},{"key":"ref4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","unstructured":"Droznin, D.V., & Droznina, S.Y. (2011). Interactive DIMAS program for processing seismic signals. Seismic Instruments, 47(3), 215. DOI: 10.3103\/ S0747923911030054","DOI":"10.3103\/s0747923911030054"},{"key":"ref5","unstructured":"Earthquakes Catalogue for Kamchatka and the Commander Islands (1962-present). (2022). Seismological Data Information System KB GS RAS. Retrieved from http:\/\/sdis.emsd.ru\/info\/earthquakes\/catalogue.php"},{"key":"ref6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Emter, D. (1997). Tidal Phenomena. In Lecture Notes in Earth Sciences, Vol. 66. Springer Berlin, Heidelberg, 400 p. DOI: 10.1007\/BFb0011453","DOI":"10.1007\/BFb0011453"},{"key":"ref7","unstructured":"Fedotov, S.A. (1982). [On the intrusion of dikes and the mechanism of fissure eruptions]. Vulkanologiia i seismologiia [Volcanology and Seismology], 5, 79-95. (In Russ.)."},{"key":"ref8","unstructured":"Fedotov, S.A. (2006). Magmaticheskie pitaiushchie sistemy i mekhanizm izverzhenii vulkanov [Magmatic Feeding Systems and the Mechanism of Volcanic Eruptions]. Moscow, Russia: Nauka Publ., 455 p. (In Russ.)."},{"key":"ref9","unstructured":"Fedotov, S.A., & Masurenkov, Iu.P. (eds.). (1991). Deistvuiushchie vulkany Kamchatki. V 2-kh t. T. 1 [Active volcanoes of Kamchatka. Vol. 1]. Moscow, Russia: Nauka Publ., 304 p. (In Russ.)."},{"key":"ref10","unstructured":"Guralp. (2022). Seismometers. Surface seismometers and accelerometers. Retrieved from http:\/\/www.guralp.com"},{"key":"ref11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","unstructured":"Khabituev, D.S., Shpynev, B.G., Tatarnikov, A.V., & Shcheglova, E.S. (2017). [Influence of the gravitational tide of the Sun and the Moon on the dynamics of the parameters of the atmosphere, ionosphere and ocean.]. Sovremennye problemy distantsionnogo zondirovaniia Zemli iz kosmosa [Current problems in remote sensing of the Earth from space], 14(5), 321-339. (In Russ.).","DOI":"10.21046\/2070-7401-2017-14-5-321-339"},{"key":"ref12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","unstructured":"McNutt, S.R., & Beavan, R.J. (1981). Volcanic earthquakes at Pavlof volcano correlated with the solid earth tide. Nature, 294, 615-618. Neuberg, J. (2000). External modulation of volcanic activity. Geophysical Journal International, 142(1), 232- 240. DOI: 10.1046\/j.1365-246x.2000.00161.x","DOI":"10.1038\/294615a0"},{"key":"ref13","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","unstructured":"Shevchenko, Yu.V. (2019). [Registration of acceleration by the mass displacement channel of the 3TB seismometer]. Vestnik KRAUNTs. Fiziko-matematicheskie nauki [Bulletin KRAESC. Physical and Mathematical Sciences\u00bb], 29(4), 218-222. (In Russ.). DOI: 10.26117\/2079-6641- 2019-29-4-218-222. EDN: NBQWFA","DOI":"10.26117\/2079-6641-2019-29-4-218-222"},{"key":"ref14","unstructured":"Slezin, Yu.B. (1998). Mekhanizm vulkanicheskikh izverzhenii (statsionarnaia model) [Mechanism of volcanic eruptions (stationary model)]. Moscow, Russia: Nauchnyi Mir Publ., 127 p. (In Russ.)."}],"container-title":["Russian Journal of Seismology"],"language":"ru","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,28]],"date-time":"2023-03-28T11:32:39Z","timestamp":1680003159000},"score":25.619896,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/www.gsras.ru\/rjs\/uploads\/files\/2022-05-01\/rus\/06.pdf"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,21]]},"references-count":15,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,21]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,21]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.35540\/2686-7907.2023.1.06","archive":["Internet Archive"],"ISSN":["2686-7907"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2686-7907","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,21]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,2]],"date-time":"2026-02-02T16:49:47Z","timestamp":1770050987279,"version":"3.49.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Akademizdatcenter Nauka","issue":"4","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>This work presents results of studying sublimates (mineral phases deposited from volcanic gases) that were collected in silica glass tubes placed in high-temperature fumaroles at the Eastern fumarole field of Avachinsky volcano (Kamchatka) in 2013\u20132023. The concentration distributions of 62 elements along the length of the tubes (along the temperature gradient) were studied by ICP-MS and ICP-AES methods. 35 phases of sublimates corresponding to natural minerals and 7 phases of sublimates for which no natural analogues are known were diagnosed. A general mineral sequence with decreasing temperature is as follows: Na and K halides; Na, K, Ca sulfates; sulfides; X-ray amorphous As-S glass and Tl, Pb, Bi halides. The most common phases are As-S glass, SiO, NaCl, KCl, NaSO\u2013KSO; rare phases are KCdCl, KPb(SO), Tl(I,Cl,Br), PbTl(Cl,I,Br), PbTl(Cl,I,Br), Pb(Cl,I,Br), TlBiI, ReS, Pb-Zn-Cd-In sulfides and AgI.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.7868\/s3034513825040028","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,10]],"date-time":"2025-11-10T17:51:45Z","timestamp":1762797105000},"page":"22","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["PHASE AND CHEMICAL COMPOSITION OF HIGH-TEMPERATURE SUBLIMATES OF AVACHINSKY VOLCANO (KAMCHATKA)"],"prefix":"10.7868","author":[{"given":"E.Yu.","family":"Plutakhina","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"4687","container-title":["\u0412\u0443\u043b\u043a\u0430\u043d\u043e\u043b\u043e\u0433\u0438\u044f \u0438 \u0441\u0435\u0439\u0441\u043c\u043e\u043b\u043e\u0433\u0438\u044f \/ Journal of Volcanology and Seismology"],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,2]],"date-time":"2026-02-02T07:13:41Z","timestamp":1770016421000},"score":25.283844,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/volcanras.ru\/s30345138s0203030625040028-1-ru\/?version_id=122664"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"4","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]}},"alternative-id":["1"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7868\/s3034513825040028","ISSN":["3034-5138"],"issn-type":[{"value":"3034-5138","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]],"date-time":"2026-08-31T20:20:46Z","timestamp":1788207646551,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media LLC","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]],"date-time":"2026-08-31T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1788134400000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc-nd\/4.0"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]],"date-time":"2026-08-31T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1788134400000},"content-version":"am","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc-nd\/4.0"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100006769","name":"Russian Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["\u2116 25-24-01182, https:\/\/rscf.ru\/project\/25-24-01182\/"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["\u2116 25-24-01182, https:\/\/rscf.ru\/project\/25-24-01182\/"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100006769","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["link.springer.com"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Sci Rep"],"DOI":"10.1038\/s41598-026-69297-6","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]],"date-time":"2026-08-31T19:36:23Z","timestamp":1788204983000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/springer_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Microfungi of volcanic thermal environments of Avachinsky volcano (Kamchatka Peninsula, Russian Far East)"],"prefix":"10.1038","author":[{"given":"Kirtsideli I.","family":"Yu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"N. S.","family":"Nikolaev","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"V. A.","family":"Iliushin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"A. P.","family":"Korablev","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"K.","family":"Arapov","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"E.","family":"Sandalova","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"D. Y.","family":"Vlasov","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"297","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]]},"container-title":["Scientific Reports"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.nature.com\/articles\/s41598-026-69297-6","content-type":"text\/html","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]],"date-time":"2026-08-31T19:36:23Z","timestamp":1788204983000},"score":22.38245,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.nature.com\/articles\/s41598-026-69297-6"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]]},"references-count":0,"alternative-id":["69297"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1038\/s41598-026-69297-6","ISSN":["2045-2322"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2045-2322","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,31]]},"assertion":[{"value":"12 June 2026","order":1,"name":"received","label":"Received","group":{"name":"ArticleHistory","label":"Article History"}},{"value":"26 August 2026","order":2,"name":"accepted","label":"Accepted","group":{"name":"ArticleHistory","label":"Article History"}},{"value":"31 August 2026","order":3,"name":"first_online","label":"First Online","group":{"name":"ArticleHistory","label":"Article History"}},{"value":"The authors declare no competing interests.","order":1,"name":"Ethics","label":"Competing interests","group":{"name":"EthicsHeading","label":"Declarations"}}]},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,3]],"date-time":"2026-10-03T00:56:17Z","timestamp":1790988977588,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":40,"publisher":"Pleiades Publishing Ltd","issue":"3","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,5,1]],"date-time":"2021-05-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1619827200000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.springernature.com\/gp\/researchers\/text-and-data-mining"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,5,1]],"date-time":"2021-05-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1619827200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.springernature.com\/gp\/researchers\/text-and-data-mining"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["link.springer.com"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["J. Volcanolog. Seismol."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2021,5]]}